Z||000013||Black88GT||11-12-2000||03:20 PM||||welcome to the forum!  Good luck on your resto project! some tips for new users...<P>1. Before you post any questions general in nature (like "what is the best exhaust" or something), use the search function.  99% of the time you will find your answer and more.  As a side note, if everyone did this I bet it would cut the number of posts in half.  Oh well...<P>2. I noticed you said you forgot something in your opening post (the pronunciation of your handle), you can "edit" the post so that you don't need to post again .  The only difference this makes is that it will say on the bottom of your edited post that you did in fact edit the post and the date it was edited.<P>just some helpful hints...<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||stimpy||11-12-2000||07:03 PM||||Whatsamatta Jeff, too <B>many</B> threads for you? Being that everything has been said and done before, should we just make this a read only archive?<BR>Really, there is no such thing as a stupid question, and bringing up a topic that has been gone down before will only bring new insight to the subject. As a hardcore forum junkie, I crave new topics being posted, and if I remember a certain thread that I have read in the past year, I will look that thread up and link it in the new topic. ||||reg||1
